Article 76 An e-commerce business operator that violates the provisions of this Law and commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the market regulatory department to make corrections within a specified period, and may be fined not more than 10,000 yuan; for an e-commerce platform operator, it shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of paragraph 1 of Article 81 of this Law:
(1) failing to display business license information, administrative license information, information on circumstances where registration as a market entity is not required, or link identifiers of the aforesaid information, in a prominent position on the homepage;
(2) failing to continuously display, in a prominent position on the homepage, the relevant information on the termination of the e-commerce business;
(3) failing to clearly specify the methods and procedures for inquiring, correcting, and deleting user information and for user deregistration, or setting unreasonable conditions for inquiring, correcting, and deleting user information and for user deregistration.
Where an e-commerce platform operator fails to take necessary measures against an operator on the platform that violates the provisions of the preceding paragraph, the market regulatory department shall order it to make corrections within a specified period, and may impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan and not more than 100,000 yuan.

Article 80 Where an e-commerce platform operator commits any of the following acts, the relevant competent authorities shall order it to rectify within a time limit; if it fails to rectify within the time limit, it shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, it shall be ordered to suspend operations for rectification and shall also be fined not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan:
(1) failing to perform the verification and registration obligations prescribed in Article 27 of this Law;
(2) failing to submit relevant information to the market regulatory department or the tax authority in accordance with Article 28 of this Law;
(3) failing to take necessary measures against illegal situations in accordance with Article 29 of this Law, or failing to report to the relevant competent authorities;
(4) failing to perform the obligation of preserving commodity and service information and transaction information prescribed in Article 31 of this Law.
Where laws or administrative regulations provide otherwise for penalties for the illegal acts specified in the preceding paragraph, those provisions shall prevail.

Article 81 Where an e-commerce platform operator violates the provisions of this Law by committing any of the following acts, the market regulatory department shall order it to rectify within a time limit and may impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, it shall be fined not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan:
(1) failing to continuously display at a prominent position on the homepage the platform service agreement, transaction rules, or link identifiers of the said information;
(2) modifying the transaction rules without publicly soliciting opinions at a prominent position on the homepage, failing to announce the modification content in advance within the prescribed time, or preventing businesses on the platform from withdrawing;
(3) failing to clearly mark and distinguish its own operations from those carried out by businesses on the platform in a prominent manner;
(4) failing to provide consumers with a channel for evaluating the goods sold or services provided on the platform, or unilaterally deleting consumers' evaluations.
Where an e-commerce platform operator violates Article 40 of this Law by failing to clearly mark goods or services subject to bidding ranking as "advertisement", it shall be penalized in accordance with the provisions of the Advertising Law of the People's Republic of China.
